NNAAMMEE
     iiddeenntt — identify RCS keyword strings in files

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     iiddeenntt [--qqVV] [_f_i_l_e _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iiddeenntt program searches for the pattern $keyword:... $ from the _f_i_l_e_s
     specified as argument (or standard input if none are given).  See the
     KEYWORD SUBSTITUTION section of rcs(1) for more information.

     The following options are supported:

     --qq   Quiet mode: suppress warnings if no pattern found.

     --VV   Display version information and exit.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The iiddeenntt utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Given the following source code in file _f_o_o_._c:

           #include <stdio.h>

           static char const rcsid[] =
                   "$Id: foo.c,v 1.2 2005/11/18 09:34:51 xsa Exp $";

           int
           main(void) {
                   printf("%s\n", rcsid);
                   return (0);
           }

     Compile it and run iiddeenntt:

           $ ident foo.c foo.o
           foo.c:
                $Id: foo.c,v 1.2 2005/11/18 09:34:51 xsa Exp $
           foo.o:
                $Id: foo.c,v 1.2 2005/11/18 09:34:51 xsa Exp $

